<PageTitle>War on Wolves</PageTitle>

<h1>War on Wolves</h1>

<section>
    <h2>European Settlers in North America</h2>
    <p>European settlers brought their own cultural attitudes about predatory species such as wolves with them to the New World. The driving force behind this hostile relationship between humans and wolves was the fight over natural resources in the form of livestock [<NavLink href="#1">1</NavLink>]. For the settlers, their horses, cattle, sheep, and pigs were critical sources of food and transportation. Likewise, the wolves saw these livestock as valuable prey due to the relative ease of hunting docile farm animals.</p>
    <img src="https://www.pbs.org/wnet/nature/files/2008/11/610_lobo_wolf-wars.jpg" alt="A group of men sitting in front of the corpses of hunted wolves" />
</section>

